* SN7400 behavioral model for Ten-Tec assembly 80308
* Pin order follows the 14-pin package:
* 1A 1B 1Y 2A 2B 2Y GND 3Y 3A 3B 4Y 4A 4B VCC
*
* This is a functional, fitted model, not a Texas Instruments transistor-level
* macromodel.  It preserves TTL thresholds, finite output impedance, propagation
* delay, floating-input-high behavior, and approximate package supply current.
.subckt SN7400_80308 1A 1B 1Y 2A 2B 2Y GND 3Y 3A 3B 4Y 4A 4B VCC

* Unconnected TTL inputs resolve high.  The resistance is a functional stand-in
* for the input transistor bias network; it is not a measured IC parameter.
R1A 1A VCC 50k
R1B 1B VCC 50k
R2A 2A VCC 50k
R2B 2B VCC 50k
R3A 3A VCC 50k
R3B 3B VCC 50k
R4A 4A VCC 50k
R4B 4B VCC 50k

* Smooth 1.4 V TTL decision level.  The internal 10 ns pole prevents ideal
* discontinuities while remaining negligible beside the calibrator timing.
B1T N1T GND V={max(V(VCC,GND),0)*(0.026786+0.598214*(1-(0.5*(1+tanh((V(1A,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(1B,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))))}
R1D N1T N1D 1
C1D N1D GND 10n
B1O N1D 1Y I={V(N1D,1Y)/(35+1e9/(1+exp((V(VCC,GND)-1)/0.1)))}

B2T N2T GND V={max(V(VCC,GND),0)*(0.026786+0.598214*(1-(0.5*(1+tanh((V(2A,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(2B,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))))}
R2D N2T N2D 1
C2D N2D GND 10n
B2O N2D 2Y I={V(N2D,2Y)/(35+1e9/(1+exp((V(VCC,GND)-1)/0.1)))}

B3T N3T GND V={max(V(VCC,GND),0)*(0.026786+0.598214*(1-(0.5*(1+tanh((V(3A,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(3B,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))))}
R3D N3T N3D 1
C3D N3D GND 10n
B3O N3D 3Y I={V(N3D,3Y)/(35+1e9/(1+exp((V(VCC,GND)-1)/0.1)))}

B4T N4T GND V={max(V(VCC,GND),0)*(0.026786+0.598214*(1-(0.5*(1+tanh((V(4A,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))*(0.5*(1+tanh((V(4B,GND)-1.4)/0.08)))))}
R4D N4T N4D 1
C4D N4D GND 10n
B4O N4D 4Y I={V(N4D,4Y)/(35+1e9/(1+exp((V(VCC,GND)-1)/0.1)))}

* Typical-order package current so the board's 5.6 V zener regulator is loaded.
BIcc VCC GND I={12m*tanh(max(V(VCC,GND),0)/0.5)}
.ends SN7400_80308
